# DVC honours this file, NOT .gitignore. Anything reachable under a stage's
# directory dependency is hashed, so a file git ignores still makes the stage
# stale -- and it does so only on the machine that lacks it. On 2026-09-13 a
# tag looked fully reproducible here and showed six stale stages on another
# clone, because these paths were being hashed into the submodule deps.

# Package-root manifests, which upstream CliMA repos do not track. Their
# CONTENT is machine-independent -- versions and tree hashes, no absolute
# paths -- so the problem is not what they contain but that a fresh clone has
# no copy, or a differently resolved one. They also do not pick the versions
# under test: the AMIP environment is experiments/AMIP/Manifest-v1.11.toml,
# which IS committed and is declared explicitly by 13 stages. These patterns
# start at */ and end at Manifest.toml, so they match neither it nor the
# superproject's own root Manifest.toml, which stays a hashed dependency.
#
# If these should be hashed instead, the fix is to commit them -- that would
# mean carrying a diff against upstream in the baseline submodules, which are
# otherwise pristine checkouts.
*/Manifest.toml
*/test/Manifest.toml
*/.dev/format/Manifest.toml

# Tooling state that lands inside a submodule checkout. The superproject's own
# .calkit/ is NOT matched: these patterns require a leading directory, and
# .calkit/notebooks/cleaned/ is a declared input to compare-kernels.
*/.calkit/
/ClimaCoupler.jl/experiments/ClimaEarth/

# Editor, OS and language scratch that varies by machine.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.cov
